description:
error.rs:36-101 — HttpError accessor methods

The wrapper exposes 8 is_* boolean methods + status() + url(). It's a clean SemVer-isolation surface.

But every caller who wants to dispatch on the error has to write:

  if http.is_timeout() || http.is_connect() {
      // retriable transient
  } else if http.is_redirect() {
      // permanent server config issue
  } else if http.is_status() {
      match http.status() {
          Some(401) | Some(403) => /* unreachable: ClientError::AuthFailed catches these */,
          Some(429) => /* retriable with backoff */,
          Some(s) if s >= 500 => /* retriable */,
          Some(_) | None => /* permanent */,
      }
  } else if http.is_body() || http.is_decode() {
      // server sent malformed bytes — permanent
  } else if http.is_builder() {
      // unreachable: caller bug, validated at construction
  } else {
      // unknown category
  }

Every caller writes this. None get it exactly right. The boolean accessors don't add up to a partition (is_status() can overlap with is_decode() depending on reqwest internals), and the caller can't tell from the docs which methods are mutually exclusive.

The right contract — and the one a JMAP retry-handling consumer needs — is a single classify() method that returns an enum:

  pub enum HttpErrorKind {
      Timeout,           // retriable
      Connect,           // retriable (often)
      Redirect,          // permanent (server config)
      Status(u16),       // dispatch on code
      RequestBody,       // caller bug
      ResponseBody,      // server bug
      Decode,            // server bug
      Builder,           // caller bug (unreachable for this crate)
      Other,
  }

A consumer-side helper would let every caller call `.classify()` once and pattern-match on the enum. The current shape forces the caller to write defensive dispatch code over a set of boolean predicates whose mutual relationships are undocumented.

Recommendation: add HttpError::kind() -> HttpErrorKind in a future minor release. The existing is_* methods can stay for source compatibility. Same applies to WebSocketError.
